::ENG1_U04_L06_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG1.C.03] Prompt: Publication task: Share research about quiet study spaces with ninth-grade students. Which product choice best fits the audience?
{
=A. A one-page digital summary with clear headings and brief evidence. #Correct. This format is easy for students to scan and understand.
~B. A twenty-page technical report with no headings. #Incorrect. This is too dense for the stated student audience.
~C. A random list with no source information. #Incorrect. Publication needs clear organization and accurate information.
~D. A private note that no one can read. #Incorrect. A publication should be prepared for an audience.
}

::ENG1_U04_L06_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG1.C.03] Prompt: Which collaborative role best checks whether source information is accurate?
{
~A. Color chooser. #Incorrect. Color choice does not verify source accuracy.
=B. Source checker. #Correct. This role directly supports accurate research publication.
~C. Timekeeper only. #Incorrect. Timekeeping may help a team but does not check sources.
~D. Audience member. #Incorrect. The audience receives the product, not necessarily checks sources.
}

::ENG1_U04_L06_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG1.C.03] Prompt: A team says, "Everyone will do whatever." What is the main problem?
{
~A. The plan has too many clear roles. #Incorrect. The plan has no clear roles.
~B. The audience is explained too carefully. #Incorrect. The audience is not explained.
=C. Responsibilities are unclear, so collaboration may break down. #Correct. Teams need roles so work is organized.
~D. The product is already publication-ready. #Incorrect. The plan is too vague to be ready.
}

::ENG1_U04_L06_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG1.C.03] Prompt: Which heading best fits a student-facing research summary about digital announcements?
{
~A. Random Information That Might Be Somewhere. #Incorrect. This heading is vague and unhelpful.
~B. Things and Stuff. #Incorrect. This does not guide the reader.
~C. The Longest Heading Ever About Every School Topic. #Incorrect. This is unfocused and too broad.
=D. How Digital Announcements Help Students Notice Club Deadlines. #Correct. This heading is specific and audience-friendly.
}

::ENG1_U04_L06_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG1.W.04] Prompt: Draft: "Our product will tell people stuff about tutoring." Which revision is clearest?
{
~A. Our product has tutoring and people and stuff. #Incorrect. This remains vague.
=B. Our one-page summary will explain how peer tutoring can support student confidence. #Correct. This clearly names the product, topic, and purpose.
~C. It will be about things students do. #Incorrect. This is too general.
~D. We will make a thing for some audience. #Incorrect. This does not identify the product or audience clearly.
}
